Cell["\<\
Usually the names of rules depend on the configuration, such as ECA or B3/S23 \
in life, but all rules can be defined as a decimal number. Since here we are \
going to study rules that belong to different spaces, it is necessary to \
distinguish the origin of each one of them. To start, we will use the \
following notation:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.6992697457019463`*^9, {3.704547447744219*^9, 3.70454745807546*^9}, {
   3.99153124341765*^9, 
   3.991531254398942*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"75e20c01-95a8-463f-91b1-\
601f8a9387c9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 SubscriptBox["rule", 
  RowBox[{"states", ",", "neighbourhood"}]]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"0e827544-0588-4b01-b9b1-90b5b529d232"]
}, Open  ]],

